/-- p27061 — 27:C18. Commutation and the internal frame: a matrix over $K$ that commutes with the two unipotent frame moves on the frame plane $V$, or on its symmetric square, which is space, is a scalar. On $V\otimes K^{r}$ and on $\mathrm{Sym}^{2}(V)\otimes K^{r}$ a commuting matrix is $1\otimes A$, for every $r$. Commutation separates the internal frame from the plane and from space, and it fixes no rank. -/
